{"id":"a011841692e719f61957329b2976fc1282b64977b33a8ac7b38b4a23465225b2","at":"2026-10-06T04:43:19Z","commit":"8dc1b0a1aa54fe46fbd27c668bcdb0eeab11a569","parents":["b3e99043b0d5b2ccd44d3d14c0ab96a407521a9e452fbcc29ddd6bf683bb6d0a"],"op":"relate","type":"verifies","ends":[{"kind":"test","id":"Depdep.SweepTest: current roots — the rail against the operator being wrong: no roots at all is a refusal, not an empty live set","hash":"554077dc"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/08-reclamation.md#sweep-refuses-without-roots","hash":"8df3c407"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"The hint says a listing with no current roots sweeps nothing and the refusal points at --report. The test asserts current_roots/2 returns {:refuse, reason} on a listing holding only an aged object, which is both halves: the refusal itself, and that it carries a reason the CLI appends the --report pointer to.","basis":"review"}
{"id":"dc3b27e0a42bfee43f119e52d439f2845c9f168f45aa3c5828ab2d4b1310d66e","at":"2026-10-06T04:43:22Z","commit":"8dc1b0a1aa54fe46fbd27c668bcdb0eeab11a569","parents":["e6155442712f935654ec77be032bf18c8861ed1ac59f3729c07af47234741aeb"],"op":"relate","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"Depdep.Sweep","hash":"e582e705"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/08-reclamation.md#rails","hash":"806d8a6c"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Reviewed sweep/1 against the three rails after #150 changed it: the change adds one guard BEFORE the listing and leaves all three intact — no --confirm still takes dry_run_summary, --grace still reaches Sweep.plan/3 untouched, and current_roots is still consulted after the listing. This test asserts the third, which sweep/1 delegates and the section calls the most important.","basis":"review"}
